# The I/L's fourth class node and the branch's single-target nuke: an orb that
# rides one enemy and shocks it thirty times over ten seconds, 871% for eight
# lines per shock at max, with a current arcing off each shock for 513% on four
# more.
#
# GMS's wording is the worst in the book, and none of it works read literally.
# "Stunned #attackCount times" means eight LINES of one shock, not eight shocks.
# The current isn't periodic and isn't a burn: it fires once per shock, four
# lines at once. What the client actually holds: 30 shocks (`x`) on a 330ms beat
# (`subTime`; the shock's hit animation runs 360ms, so shocks land back to
# back), each 391+16x on `mobCount 1`, and a separate invisible skill for the
# current at 243+9x, `attackCount 4`, `mobCount 2`. `time 40000` is the orb's
# forty-second lifetime, which only matters if the barrage pauses to hop between
# kills.
#
# The orb hops between enemies while any are standing, which needs positions
# this game doesn't have, so it hits the front of the queue and moves on when
# that one dies. On a boss, which the skill is for, it is the same: the orb
# stays on it for all thirty, which is what KMS values the skill for.
#
# The stun is one of the three statuses this game tracks on monsters. Nothing
# here has a schedule to interrupt, so what it gives is that the enemy is
# AFFLICTED, which Storm Magic checks, and that other lightning then does 12%
# more, as GMS states, excluding this skill by name. Bosses are never stunned,
# so in the fight it was built for only the 12% remains.
#
# The four seconds are OUR choice: GMS states no stun duration in the common
# block, and a missing number there means the client hardcodes one. Each shock
# applies its own, and the thirty come 330ms apart, so the mark lasts the whole
# barrage and four seconds after, whatever the number. It really only decides
# how long the rest of the book gets the 12% afterwards.
#
# The 3.4s refunded per unused shock matters on MAPS, not bosses. Against a boss
# the orb uses all thirty and refunds nothing; on a map it kills what it rides
# and outlasts the crowd, so the leftover shocks come off the next cooldown.
name: "Jupiter Thunder"
description:
  "Launch orbs full of the thunder god's power directly at your enemies. "
  "The orb goes inside the enemy it touched to deal continuous shock damage. "
  "Enemies touched by the orb are stunned. An electric current flows around "
  "that enemy to attack others."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
tags: SKILL_TAG_LIGHTNING
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_ICE_LIGHTNING_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 4 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_STAFF
base_delay_ms: 810
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
cooldown_refund_seconds: 3.4
max_enemies: 1
lines: 8
freeze_lines_per_spend: 5
stun {
  duration_seconds: 4.0
  final_dmg_pct: 0.12
  lifted_tag: SKILL_TAG_LIGHTNING
}
casts: 30
cast_interval_ms: 330
base { skill_pct: 4.07 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.16 }
extra_hit {
  label: "Electric Current"
  max_enemies: 2
  lines: 4
  base { skill_pct: 2.52 }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.09 }
}
